.\" Title: vrw-cert-list
.\" Author: vrw contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\" Process this file with
.\"   groff -man -Tascii vrw-cert-list.1

.TH VRW\-CERT\-LIST 1 "2025" "vrw" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrw\-cert\-list \- list all certificates in the certificate pool

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrw
\fBcert list\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
List all certificates configured in the vrw certificate pool. The output reads from the configuration file (global \fB~/.config/vrw/config.yaml\fR or local \fB./vrw.yaml\fR) and displays each certificate's name, file paths, and the first 16 characters of its derived bearer token.

The certificate pool provides per-command access control. Each certificate has a derived bearer token (SHA-256 of the certificate PEM), and commands can be bound to a specific certificate. When a certificate-bound command receives an API request, it checks that the request's bearer token matches the certificate's derived token.

This subcommand is synchronous and does not require a running vrw instance. It only reads the configuration file to display registered certificate entries.

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
List all certificates:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw cert list\fR
NAME                     CERT FILE                                         TOKEN (prefix)
my-app                   /home/user/.config/vrw/certs/my-app/cert.pem   a3f8c1e2b7d94001
ci-pipeline              /home/user/.config/vrw/certs/ci-pipeline/cert.pem 7c1e9d4a8f2...
staging                  /home/user/.config/vrw/certs/staging/cert.pem  d4e5f6a7b8c90123
.fi
.RE

.PP
Empty pool:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw cert list\fR
No certificates in pool.
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Successful listing (including empty pool).

.TP
.B 1
Error (configuration file read error, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO

